// Copy to Signing.local.xcconfig, next to this file, to sign your builds with your own
// certificate. That file is gitignored. macOS then ties Live Transcribe's permissions to the
// certificate instead of to each build, so they survive rebuilds: grant them once more after
// switching, and not again while the certificate stays the same.
//
// An Apple Development certificate is enough (Xcode › Settings › Accounts creates one, free with
// any Apple ID). List the ones you have with:
//     security find-identity -v -p codesigning
// The team ID is the certificate's organizational unit, also shown under Accounts.

CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID
